 regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After rollback the service reports healthy with error rate 0.2% in all regions. Follow-up: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression before re-deploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 51099, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01YEunZ4WExiyiVJjEwSCk7V", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 51099, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01YEunZ4WExiyiVJjEwSCk7V", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 55178, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n1. **Problem:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0. A follow-up status check shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api). It says what failed, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery numbers, and a follow-up to find the cause of the v2.3.1 problem before it's deployed again.\n   - The first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops a request from running twice. There's only one incident and one page.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MfYLrrY1MWhM1ofiRyvK6x", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_ser