lu_01YEunZ4WExiyiVJjEwSCk7V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the deploy of v2.3.1 (unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west; error rate 18%). The preceding v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. After rollback the service reports healthy with error rate 0.2% in all regions. Follow-up: root-cause the v2.3.1 regression before re-deploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident, which paged on-call.\n\n1. **Problem:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The release candidate before it, v2.3.1-rc, had also been unhealthy, so the most recent healthy release was v2.3.0.\n2. **Rollback:** All three regions now run v2.3.0. A follow-up status check shows the service healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n3. **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api). It says what failed, the rollback to v2.3.0, the recovery numbers, and a follow-up to find the cause of the v2.3.1 problem before it's deployed again.\n   - The first attempt to create it timed out. The incident list was still empty afterwards, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops a request from running twice. There's only one incident and one page.", "type": "text"}]}]}